Part 3. Drift Angle

You need to assess the drift angle status for the Beacon. Q.U.A. tells you the formula for drift angle:
θradians=arctanverticalhorizontal


    Prompt the user for:
        Horizontal beacon offset (in km)
        Vertical beacon offset (in km)
        NOTE: These are floats

    If the horizontal drift is zero, print that the beacon is too unstable to calculate drift, set the status to undefined and the angle to -99999

    Otherwise, calculate the drift angle and determine the drift status

    Depending on the angle, the drift status will be:
    Angle (°) 	Status
    θ < 10 	acceptable
    10 ≤ θ < 25 	elevated
    25 ≤ θ 	excessive


    Example values:

Horizontal (km) 	Vertical (km) 	Angle (°) 	Status
0 	any value 	-99999 	undefined
21.936 	2.114 	5.505 	acceptable
52.782 	18.224 	19.048 	elevated
5.7 	112.9 	87.110 	excessive

        CK will warn you of the status
        Save the angle value and status for the report in Part 5



Part 4. Signal Degradation

You need to assess the how much the beacon signal has degraded. Q.U.A. tells you the formula for signal degradation:

LossdB=10⋅log10PfinalPinitial


        Prompt the user for initial and final beacon power. These are floats

        If the initial signal is zero, print that the signal strength too small to calculate signal, set the status to undefined and the degradation to -99999

        Otherwise, calculate the signal loss and determine the signal status

        Depending on the loss, the signal status will be:

Signal Status 	Threshold (dB) 	Description
Minimal 	0 down to -3 dB 	Negligible effect on signal; communication is clear.
Acceptable 	-3 down to -10 dB 	Some degradation; still usable, but may require monitoring.
Significant 	-10 down to -20 dB 	Noticeable impact on performance; communication may be unreliable.
Critical 	-20 dB and below 	Severe loss; likely no signal received; immediate attention required.

        Example values:

Pinitial 	Pfinal 	Loss (dB) 	Status
0 	any value 	-99999 	undefined
3982.382 	3805.776 	-0.1970 	minimal
4988.717 	732.149 	-8.3339 	acceptable
5733.56 	509.281 	-10.5147 	significant
8912.992 	55.312 	-22.0720 	critical

        CK will warn you of the status
        Save the loss value and status for the report in Part 5



Part 5. Beacon Report

Output the Beacon Station report.

        The report must include:
            The station name
            The intern name
            The employee ID
            The drift angle (3 decimals) and status
            The signal degradation (4 decimals) and status

        Statuses must be uppercase

        Category is left aligned

        Data is right aligned

        Example:

    ========================================
            Apogee-17 Beacon Report         
    ========================================
      Technician:                 Juno Lee
      Employee ID:             27389298378
    ========================================
      Drift Angle:              88.282 deg
      Drift Status:              EXCESSIVE
    ========================================
      Signal Degradation:      -22.2189 dB
      Signal status:              CRITICAL
    ========================================



